# CashFly — Cursor Project Rules

## What This Project Is
CashFly is a cash-leak detection tool for Pretty Fly (fictional DTC streetwear brand).
It's built for a 3-day hackathon (Wayflyer × Fin, London, June 3–5 2026).

**The single job:** Find stuck cash in inventory, supplier POs, and ad spend.
**The single constraint:** All numbers must reconcile against bank_transactions.csv.

## Architecture
- `backend/` — FastAPI + pandas (Python 3.11)
- `frontend/` — Next.js 14 App Router + Tailwind + shadcn/ui
- `data/` — Pretty Fly CSVs (21 files, gitignored)
- `docs/` — PRD, TRD, SE specs (read these before building anything)

## The Golden Rule
**pandas computes, Claude explains.**
Never ask the LLM to calculate £ amounts. Compute in Python first.
Pass computed values to Claude as context for natural language generation only.

## "Today" in This Dataset
The dataset window is June 2024 → May 2026.
"Today" = `2026-06-01`. Use this constant everywhere.
```python
DATASET_TODAY = date(2026, 6, 1)
```

## What We Are NOT Building
- No AI executive team / board meeting
- No What-If simulator
- No multi-user auth
- No real database — all in-memory pandas DataFrames
- No mobile optimization

## Code Style
- Python: type hints everywhere, docstrings on all public functions
- TypeScript: strict mode, no `any`
- Commits: conventional commits (feat/fix/chore)
- Error messages: user-facing, plain English, never expose stack traces
